{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And they shall be for lights, etc.</b> The simple meaning of the verse tells that HaShem commanded that the light of the luminaries should pierce through the heavens, and further that it illuminate the earth — meaning that the luminaries shine throughout the entire expanse of the heavens and also their light reaches down below to the earth. It further intends that HaShem prepared them so that the intensity of their light shine in the firmament, and from the light that spreads through the firmament the earth be illuminated, for the earth has no capacity to bear the intensity of the luminaries' light directly. This is what He was precise in saying <b>for lights in the firmament of the heavens</b> — meaning that there they shine — and in saying <b>to illuminate upon the earth</b> — meaning that from the light shining in the firmament the earth is illuminated." "And according to their words, their memory for blessing (Ḥagigah 12b), that the luminaries are in the firmament — specifically two things: the source of the luminaries' light pierces only in the heavens, and the heavens themselves illuminate the earth. And what they said, their memory for blessing (Yoma 28b): ״יוֹמָא דְּעֵיבָא כּוּלֵּיהּ שִׁמְשָׁא״ (on a cloudy day the sun prevails throughout), does not contradict our words, for in any event the place of the sun, even though the sun's intensity spreads to the sides, there is a difference between the place of the sun's fixed position, which has greater intensity than its surroundings. And יוֹמָא דְּעֵיבָא — the sun turns back a second time and the sun's remaining intensity, directed toward the earth, spreads to a measure the earth can bear, then turns and spreads through the height of the heavens by means of the clouds — and that is ״כּוּלֵּיהּ שִׁמְשָׁא״."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {1 "The Aramaic phrase יוֹמָא דְּעֵיבָא כּוּלֵּיהּ שִׁמְשָׁא (literally 'a day of cloud, all of it is sun') is left in original Aramaic as it is a direct quotation from the Talmud."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T18:55:55.194282714Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}